<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40194" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quinquĕrēmis</span></b> ,
		is, adj.
		quinque-remus: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decem quinqueremes naves,</span>”
				<i>having five banks of oars</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					41, 9, 1</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quinquĕrēmis</span></b> , is,
				f., <i>a ship</i> or <i>galley having five banks of oars</i>, <i>a
				quinquereme</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in quinqueremi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 46, § 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">una,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					42, 48</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">37, 12</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				7, 56, 57, § 208</span></i>.</div>
